  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nMonsoonal flow will continue to bring shower and thunderstorm \nchances for the Silver State through the middle of next week. \nModels show a daily 20% to 50% chance of isolated to scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms. Storm modes at this time favor wet \nstorm modes for central and eastern Nevada. However, for western \nNevada from about Battle Mountain and points west, there will \nstill be a chance for a few dry thunderstorms, or for storms that \nhave very little in the way of accumulating precipitation. Common \nhazard for storms will include gusty outflow winds up to 50 MPH, \nground lightning strikes, and brief heavy rainfall. Will need to \nwatch central Nevada burn scars as recent fires an hydrophobic \nsoils may lead to flash flooding concerns if cells are slower \nmoving. After Wednesday, models show that the upper ridge will try\nand work its way back west and shifting the upper flow back to a \nWSW direction, thus cutting off moisture flow by Thursday of next \nweek. There may be a low chance for thunder on Thursday and Friday\ndepending on how much residue moisture can stick around. \nTemperatures will be on a cooling trend as the surge of moisture \nand the displacement of the ridge will allow highs to cool back \ninto the low 80s to low 90s, or cooler if you see a thundershower.\nOvernight lows will be dropping into the mid 50s to mid 60s \ngiving a nice break from the recent heat. Winds will be breezy \nthrough the weekend and into the new week as winds shift more \nsouth to southwest in line with the upper level flow pattern at \nspeeds of 10 to 20 MPH with gusts up to 30 MPH possible. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for the return of southerly flow and \nmonsoonal moisture beginning Friday afternoon, bringing a daily \n20% to 50% chance for isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms for Nevada through Wednesday. \n     \nThere is low to medium confidence of upper pattern evolution \nafter Wednesday as models show a weakening of the monsoon flow as \nthe upper level ridge returns to the west bringing warmer \ntemperatures.",
